    "text": "> If the checksum does not include the pseudo header, a user datagram may arrive safe and sound. > If IP header is corrupted, it may be delivered to the wrong host. > The protocol field is added to ensure that the packet belongs to UDP. > The value of the protocol field for UDP is 17. > If this value is changed during transmission, the checksum calculation at the receiver will detect it and UDP drops the packet. It 1s not delivered to the wrong protocol.",
